    <statement><p>Determine the global extreme values of the function on the given set without using calculus</p>
<p><m>f(x,y)=2e^{-\left(5x^{2}+8y^{2}\right)}, \quad 5x^{2}+8y^{2} \le 1</m></p>
<p><m>f_{min}=</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>f_{max}=</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.735759</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f(x,y)=\frac{1}{e^{5x^{2}+8y^{2}}}</m> occurs when <m>e^{5x^{2}+8y^{2}}</m> is minimum, that is, when <m>5x^{2}+8y^{2}</m> is minimum. 


The minimum value of <m>5x^{2}+8y^{2}</m> on the given set is zero. Therefore <m>f_{max}=2 e^{-0}=2</m>.



The minimum value of <m>f</m> occurs when <m>5x^{2}+8y^{2}</m> is maximum, that is, when <m>5x^{2}+8y^{2}=1</m>. 


Thus, the minimum value of <m>f</m> on the given set is obtained on the boundary, and its value <m>f_{min}=2 e^{-1}</m>





</solution>
